WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.535
Welcome to the Estate Aegis tutorial.

2
00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.253
The smarter way to manage private residences.

3
00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:12.863
We will follow a family from its first record through residence setup,
inspections, arrival preparation, and daily operations.

4
00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:15.399
The login screen has three portal choices.

5
00:00:15.399 --> 00:00:21.922
Admin is for managing the workspace, Client is for the family's experience,
and Vendor is for assigned jobs.

6
00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:24.580
Use the portal associated with your account.

7
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.411
Here we enter our demonstration administrator's email and password, then log
in.

8
00:00:29.411 --> 00:00:35.270
If you have enabled two-factor authentication, enter your authenticator or
recovery code as well.

9
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.618
After signing in, begin on Overview.

10
00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:44.586
Your company's name appears on the left, with its logo beside Powered by
Estate Aegis in the header.

11
00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:50.733
Open Action needed to see outstanding items, and scroll through the page to
review the dashboard tiles.

12
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:53.120
The tiles lead to the connected records.

13
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.252
Work needing attention and Completed inspection reports can each expand
independently.

14
00:00:58.252 --> 00:01:02.311
Individual work cards also expand, so you can keep the page compact.

15
00:01:02.311 --> 00:01:07.622
Counts remain visible when sections are closed, and overdue items are
highlighted in red.

16
00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:11.680
This is your starting point for deciding what needs attention today.

17
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.659
Before adding clients, open Company settings from Administration.

18
00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:24.217
In the settings form, check the company name, enter your support email, and
select the main administrator for email notifications.

19
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:29.798
Upload your company logo and use the available plain-background removal
option when appropriate.

20
00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.252
Preview it before saving.

21
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:39.857
These settings give the workspace your identity: your company name on the
sidebar, your logo in the header, and your branding on inspection reports.

22
00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:42.764
The report footer carries Powered by Estate Aegis.

23
00:01:42.764 --> 00:01:46.659
You can return here whenever your branding or main contact changes.

24
00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:48.810
Save settings when you are satisfied.

25
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.303
To start using the software, create the family first.

26
00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:57.962
Open Residences and Clients, choose Client families, and select Add family.

27
00:01:57.962 --> 00:02:01.130
Here we enter Jordan Morgan as the primary contact.

28
00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.858
Check the family name, then enter an email and phone number.

29
00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:09.766
Scroll down to enter the street address, city, state, postal code, and
country.

30
00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:14.550
The family is the household record; it can connect to one or more
residences.

31
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.662
Review the fields and select Save.

32
00:02:16.662 --> 00:02:25.670
We now have the Morgan family profile, which brings the contact details and
address together and gives us a starting point for adding their home.

33
00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.810
From the family profile, choose Add this address as a residence.

34
00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.443
Give the home a clear name, such as Morgan Beach Residence.

35
00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:39.676
The family and address carry into the form, so check those details before
continuing.

36
00:02:39.676 --> 00:02:42.262
Scroll down to Residence rooms and spaces.

37
00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:46.633
Select Add room or space for each area you want your team to recognize.

38
00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:54.514
For this example, we add a primary suite, record its floor, and enter
preparation notes about fresh linens and cooling the room.

39
00:02:54.514 --> 00:02:59.070
Then we add the main kitchen with its own floor and stocking instructions.

40
00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.949
Each space has a type, a name, an assignment option, and notes.

41
00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:08.798
These named areas provide useful context for inspecting the home and
preparing it for arrivals.

42
00:03:08.798 --> 00:03:12.061
Keep the room list accurate as the household changes.

43
00:03:12.061 --> 00:03:14.770
Scroll to the bottom and save the residence.

44
00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.521
Now open Residences and select View residence for Morgan Beach Residence.

45
00:03:20.521 --> 00:03:22.579
This is the home's own dashboard.

46
00:03:22.579 --> 00:03:26.632
The header identifies the family, address, and residence manager.

47
00:03:26.632 --> 00:03:29.562
Below it, the tabs organize the home's records.

48
00:03:29.562 --> 00:03:33.054
On Overview, expand a work card to review upcoming work.

49
00:03:33.054 --> 00:03:36.171
The neighboring area shows the latest inspections.

50
00:03:36.171 --> 00:03:39.101
Scroll down to reach Family members and guests.

51
00:03:39.101 --> 00:03:46.770
This puts the home's work, recent inspection, and household together,
without making you search through company-wide lists.

52
00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:52.070
You can return to this page whenever you need the context for a particular
residence.

53
00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.703
In Family members and guests, choose Add member or guest.

54
00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:00.437
We add Casey Morgan and save an email address with the record.

55
00:04:00.437 --> 00:04:05.135
An email on file lets an administrator send an invitation tied to this
family.

56
00:04:05.135 --> 00:04:12.061
Review the person's details and invitation status here, and use the
available invitation controls to manage access.

57
00:04:12.061 --> 00:04:19.227
Adding a family record alone does not mean that the person has signed in;
they still need their own account invitation.

58
00:04:19.227 --> 00:04:23.684
Removing a linked family member also suspends that person's linked access.

59
00:04:23.684 --> 00:04:27.900
Keep this list current whenever someone joins or leaves the household.

60
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.646
Next, open the residence's Inspections tab.

61
00:04:31.646 --> 00:04:37.330
Save the report recipient here once, so you do not have to enter the email
for every inspection.

62
00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:43.014
Review the next inspection due date and use Edit schedule when a saved
schedule needs to change.

63
00:04:43.014 --> 00:04:46.922
The frequency and next due date help your team plan repeat visits.

64
00:04:46.922 --> 00:04:51.777
Select Start inspection, check the residence and date, and save to open the
draft.

65
00:04:51.777 --> 00:04:53.731
A draft is the working checklist.

66
00:04:53.731 --> 00:04:58.290
It is separate from the completed, published report that the client
receives.

67
00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.310
We will walk through the results before publishing.

68
00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:06.871
Work through the walkthrough checklist and select a result for each item.

69
00:05:06.871 --> 00:05:09.081
Pass records an acceptable condition.

70
00:05:09.081 --> 00:05:11.949
Monitor highlights something to watch in yellow.

71
00:05:11.949 --> 00:05:14.219
Attention highlights a problem in red.

72
00:05:14.219 --> 00:05:20.134
Not applicable is available when an item does not apply; add an explanation
so the result is clear.

73
00:05:20.134 --> 00:05:24.674
Here we record a filter to monitor and a minor leak that requires attention.

74
00:05:24.674 --> 00:05:29.214
Add a concise observation beside the item, then continue down the checklist.

75
00:05:29.214 --> 00:05:34.292
Use the residence's rooms and preparation details as context while checking
the home.

76
00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:39.370
Clear findings make the report easier for both the family and the team to
understand.

77
00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:45.164
At the bottom of the inspection, enter Notes to the client in plain
language.

78
00:05:45.164 --> 00:05:48.863
Internal notes are separate and stay out of the client report.

79
00:05:48.863 --> 00:05:53.756
Use the inspection summary to bring the overall condition and next steps
together.

80
00:05:53.756 --> 00:05:59.185
Photo evidence belongs below the summary, and Add photos lets you attach
supporting images.

81
00:05:59.185 --> 00:06:04.018
Checklist changes and notes save automatically, and Save draft is also
available.

82
00:06:04.018 --> 00:06:09.687
If your connection drops, keep the current tab open so its changes can sync
when you reconnect.

83
00:06:09.687 --> 00:06:13.207
Uploading photos and publishing still require a connection.

84
00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:16.190
Review the entire inspection before completing it.

85
00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:22.407
When the checklist is complete, an administrator can select Complete and
publish.

86
00:06:22.407 --> 00:06:27.734
Publishing locks the inspection and starts report delivery to the saved
email address.

87
00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.336
Check the report's email status afterward.

88
00:06:30.336 --> 00:06:40.061
The PDF uses your company name and logo and includes the residence,
inspector, completion date and time in Eastern Time, findings, client notes,
and summary.

89
00:06:40.061 --> 00:06:43.096
Monitor remains yellow and Attention remains red.

90
00:06:43.096 --> 00:06:46.565
Download PDF report gives you a copy to review or share.

91
00:06:46.565 --> 00:06:51.830
Published reports preserve the completed inspection; they are not edited
like drafts.

92
00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.007
Here is the inspection PDF from our demonstration.

93
00:06:56.007 --> 00:07:00.949
Your company leads the header, while Powered by Estate Aegis appears at the
bottom.

94
00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:05.713
The inspector and completion details identify who carried out the work and
when.

95
00:07:05.713 --> 00:07:10.298
Colored findings draw the reader to the items that need monitoring or
action.

96
00:07:10.298 --> 00:07:14.585
The report finishes with the client-facing notes and inspection summary.

97
00:07:14.585 --> 00:07:16.252
Internal notes are excluded.

98
00:07:16.252 --> 00:07:24.350
Before relying on automatic delivery, confirm that the residence's recipient
address is correct and check the sending status in the app.

99
00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:29.827
Published items marked Monitor or Attention appear in Inspection follow-up.

100
00:07:29.827 --> 00:07:34.275
Choose Create work order beside a finding to create its linked follow-up
work.

101
00:07:34.275 --> 00:07:39.236
Then use View work to open the job and manage its assignment, scheduling,
and progress.

102
00:07:39.236 --> 00:07:43.228
The link keeps the original observation connected to the action taken.

103
00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:48.702
When work already exists for a finding, open that linked record instead of
creating a duplicate.

104
00:07:48.702 --> 00:07:53.150
This gives your team a clear path from inspection to follow-up and
completion.

105
00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:59.287
If you started an inspection by mistake, open the draft and choose Delete
draft.

106
00:07:59.287 --> 00:08:01.756
Read the confirmation before proceeding.

107
00:08:01.756 --> 00:08:05.891
Deleting removes the unfinished inspection and its uploaded photos.

108
00:08:05.891 --> 00:08:10.889
In this demonstration we cancel the confirmation, so the draft remains
available.

109
00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:14.592
This option is for drafts; published reports stay protected.

110
00:08:14.592 --> 00:08:22.430
Use Save draft when you intend to return to the inspection, and Delete draft
only when the unfinished record should be removed.

111
00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.295
Continue to Shopping in the residence card.

112
00:08:26.295 --> 00:08:31.004
This is the home's reusable list of preferred groceries and household items.

113
00:08:31.004 --> 00:08:35.156
Select Add item, choose a category, then select the item and brand.

114
00:08:35.156 --> 00:08:39.928
Use Other to enter a custom item or brand when the preset choices do not
fit.

115
00:08:39.928 --> 00:08:47.674
We are adding a welcome fruit basket from a local market, with a quantity
and instructions to place it on the kitchen island.

116
00:08:47.674 --> 00:08:49.223
Save it to the residence.

117
00:08:49.223 --> 00:08:55.234
You can edit or remove items later, and Import CSV or TXT provides another
way to build the list.

118
00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:59.200
Saved preferences can then be selected for a particular arrival.

119
00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.804
Move to Arrivals and select Plan arrival.

120
00:09:02.804 --> 00:09:08.784
Confirm the residence, enter the arrival date and time, and describe any
additional preparation needs.

121
00:09:08.784 --> 00:09:15.351
Review the available family or guest selections, then choose the preferred
shopping items needed for this visit.

122
00:09:15.351 --> 00:09:21.625
Here we request the welcome basket and note that the primary suite should be
cool, with fresh linens ready.

123
00:09:21.625 --> 00:09:24.967
Submit arrival creates a preparation record for the team.

124
00:09:24.967 --> 00:09:31.358
Keep visit-specific instructions here, while keeping reusable room and
shopping preferences on the residence.

125
00:09:31.358 --> 00:09:34.700
That separation makes the next arrival easier to prepare.

126
00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.548
Open the arrival from Arrival preparation to manage the visit.

127
00:09:39.548 --> 00:09:45.668
A submitted arrival creates in-app notifications for administrators and
staff assigned to the residence.

128
00:09:45.668 --> 00:09:50.023
Review the notes, then work through the selected shopping items and rooms.

129
00:09:50.023 --> 00:09:54.259
Mark every selected item purchased, and record a substitution if needed.

130
00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:57.496
Mark every room Ready after completing its preparation.

131
00:09:57.496 --> 00:10:00.732
The room names and notes come from the residence setup.

132
00:10:00.732 --> 00:10:05.970
Choose Confirm preparation is ready, then confirm that all additional tasks
are complete.

133
00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:10.912
The system checks these requirements before allowing the arrival to be
marked ready.

134
00:10:10.912 --> 00:10:15.620
Keep the statuses accurate so the family and team can check progress in the
app.

135
00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.900
Continue along the residence's top bar to Services.

136
00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.436
This view limits work to the current home.

137
00:10:22.436 --> 00:10:27.025
Expand a job to see the assignment, status, due date, and available actions.

138
00:10:27.025 --> 00:10:30.890
Use it when you already know which residence you are working on.

139
00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:37.351
Administrators can create a new work order here, while clients use their
permitted service-request options.

140
00:10:37.351 --> 00:10:43.390
We will cover notes, scheduling, and approvals in the company-wide Daily
Operations section shortly.

141
00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.167
Documents keeps files attached to this home.

142
00:10:47.167 --> 00:10:52.262
Select Upload document, choose the file, and review the document details
before saving.

143
00:10:52.262 --> 00:10:56.361
Use descriptive names so your team can recognize the right file later.

144
00:10:56.361 --> 00:11:02.334
The residence view helps you find home-specific information without browsing
every property's records.

145
00:11:02.334 --> 00:11:11.880
The separate company-wide Documents page brings permitted residence
documents together; we will point out that shortcut later without repeating
the upload process.

146
00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.626
Assets organizes the home's equipment and other tracked assets.

147
00:11:16.626 --> 00:11:20.227
Choose Add asset to see the fields for its identity and details.

148
00:11:20.227 --> 00:11:27.206
Record the information useful for servicing it, such as model information
and warranty details where the form provides them.

149
00:11:27.206 --> 00:11:33.453
Asset records can hold service history and inspections, giving your team a
reference when planning maintenance.

150
00:11:33.453 --> 00:11:39.700
Create a clear record for each item rather than relying on a general note
that will be difficult to find later.

151
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:46.095
The Residence Manager tab lets an administrator choose the person
responsible for this home.

152
00:11:46.095 --> 00:11:50.725
Select Residence Manager, choose the appropriate account, and save the
assignment.

153
00:11:50.725 --> 00:11:57.614
The manager's name then appears with the residence and in relevant work
context, including the vendor's assigned-job view.

154
00:11:57.614 --> 00:12:02.640
Keep this assignment current so questions and coordination have a clear
point of contact.

155
00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:08.698
Access and codes is the dedicated place for gate, door, alarm, and lockbox
details.

156
00:12:08.698 --> 00:12:16.835
The page explains that access is available to administrators and the
assigned residence manager, and that viewing and changes are recorded.

157
00:12:16.835 --> 00:12:20.757
Use View access details when you are authorized to open the record.

158
00:12:20.757 --> 00:12:27.430
Keep credentials in this section instead of putting them into the house
manual, general notes, or a client report.

159
00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:32.468
The Manual tab holds operating procedures for authorized staff.

160
00:12:32.468 --> 00:12:39.108
Open Edit manual to record useful instructions, such as how to prepare a
room or operate household equipment.

161
00:12:39.108 --> 00:12:43.007
Organize the text so someone arriving at the home can follow it.

162
00:12:43.007 --> 00:12:48.185
This is for procedures; gate, door, and alarm credentials belong in Access
and codes.

163
00:12:48.185 --> 00:12:52.510
Save the manual and keep it current as the household's routines change.

164
00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.302
Notes is the residence's internal note area.

165
00:12:56.302 --> 00:13:00.191
Add a note for operational context that should stay with the home.

166
00:13:00.191 --> 00:13:06.613
Use clear, specific wording so another team member can understand what
happened or what needs to happen next.

167
00:13:06.613 --> 00:13:13.978
Keep inspection findings in the inspection and job progress in the work
order, where those workflows track their own history.

168
00:13:13.978 --> 00:13:17.160
This tab completes our tour across the residence card.

169
00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:23.718
Back on the sidebar, Residences and Clients organizes the household side of
the workspace.

170
00:13:23.718 --> 00:13:30.446
Residences opens the home cards, and Client families opens the contacts and
linked homes we created at the start.

171
00:13:30.446 --> 00:13:35.805
Arrival preparation brings submitted visits together across the residences
you can access.

172
00:13:35.805 --> 00:13:44.021
The client portal also offers a Shopping list shortcut, while administrators
can manage preferred shopping directly inside each residence.

173
00:13:44.021 --> 00:13:50.570
These are connected views of the same records, so you do not need to enter
the family, home, or arrival twice.

174
00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.994
Now open Daily Operations and start with Work orders.

175
00:13:54.994 --> 00:13:57.914
This company-wide view brings the jobs together.

176
00:13:57.914 --> 00:14:02.659
Expand a card to review its residence, priority, due date, vendor, and
status.

177
00:14:02.659 --> 00:14:07.344
Add note records progress with the job, such as a confirmed technician
visit.

178
00:14:07.344 --> 00:14:14.096
Request more information keeps a question with the work and notifies the
appropriate manager and administrator.

179
00:14:14.096 --> 00:14:20.606
Other actions let you assign or schedule work, request client approval, add
a photo, and submit completion.

180
00:14:20.606 --> 00:14:26.081
Assignment and schedule emails help notify the people involved and the main
administrator.

181
00:14:26.081 --> 00:14:31.130
Keep detailed updates in the work record so the next person can follow the
history.

182
00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:35.975
Service requests captures what a client or team member needs.

183
00:14:35.975 --> 00:14:43.206
Choose Request service, select the residence, give the request a clear
title, describe the problem, and set its priority.

184
00:14:43.206 --> 00:14:49.779
Administrators can review requests, adjust priority, and create or link the
work order that will address them.

185
00:14:49.779 --> 00:14:54.919
A request states the need; the linked work record carries the assignment and
progress.

186
00:14:54.919 --> 00:14:59.520
Review existing linked work before creating another job for the same
request.

187
00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:04.819
Inspection reports is the company-wide list of inspections you can access.

188
00:15:04.819 --> 00:15:11.411
Use it to find drafts and published reports across homes, or start an
inspection after selecting the correct residence.

189
00:15:11.411 --> 00:15:16.119
The inspection process is the same one we demonstrated inside Morgan Beach
Residence.

190
00:15:16.119 --> 00:15:25.370
This view is useful when you are reviewing the day's inspection activity
across several properties, while the residence tab is useful when you are
focused on one home.

191
00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:31.379
Calendar brings dated work, inspections, and arrivals into one ordered view.

192
00:15:31.379 --> 00:15:37.265
Review the residence, date, and status beside each entry to understand the
upcoming workload.

193
00:15:37.265 --> 00:15:40.366
Overdue entries are highlighted where applicable.

194
00:15:40.366 --> 00:15:45.238
Use the underlying work, inspection, or arrival record to manage its
details.

195
00:15:45.238 --> 00:15:51.630
The calendar helps you see the timing across those workflows without keeping
a separate list by hand.

196
00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.580
Daily route helps plan visits.

197
00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:59.829
Enter a starting address, or use Locate me when you want to provide your
current location.

198
00:15:59.829 --> 00:16:07.995
Choose whether to include inspections due in the next three days and open
work orders, then review the individual residences selected below.

199
00:16:07.995 --> 00:16:09.745
Add or remove stops as needed.

200
00:16:09.745 --> 00:16:12.136
Each residence appears once in the route.

201
00:16:12.136 --> 00:16:15.519
Check the addresses before opening Google Maps directions.

202
00:16:15.519 --> 00:16:21.410
This connects your planned stops to navigation while keeping the operational
records in Estate Aegis.

203
00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:25.594
Client approvals brings spending decisions together.

204
00:16:25.594 --> 00:16:31.562
Start an approval request from the relevant work order, enter the amount,
and explain the proposed work.

205
00:16:31.562 --> 00:16:37.300
The client can approve or decline in the system, and the decision remains
recorded with the request.

206
00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:41.375
Review the decision before proceeding with work that requires approval.

207
00:16:41.375 --> 00:16:46.080
This is a record of the client's authorization, rather than a card-payment
screen.

208
00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.113
Next, open Staff and Vendors.

209
00:16:49.113 --> 00:16:54.043
The Staff page is for employment details that company administrators can
view.

210
00:16:54.043 --> 00:17:01.880
Create a staff member or edit an existing person's details, including the
contact and job information supported by the form.

211
00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:07.316
Keep those details current so the right person can be assigned to residences
and work.

212
00:17:07.316 --> 00:17:13.510
Staff profiles, schedules, and account access have separate purposes; we
will review each in turn.

213
00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:19.718
Staff schedules plans a person's time and connects it to a residence or
assignment.

214
00:17:19.718 --> 00:17:25.329
Create a schedule, select the staff member, set the start and end time, and
add instructions.

215
00:17:25.329 --> 00:17:27.622
Times use the device's local timezone.

216
00:17:27.622 --> 00:17:32.147
Use Assign work to attach work or the supported task types to the schedule.

217
00:17:32.147 --> 00:17:38.422
The person scheduled and the main administrator receive the relevant email
notification when configured.

218
00:17:38.422 --> 00:17:42.042
You can return to edit or remove a schedule as plans change.

219
00:17:42.042 --> 00:17:47.110
Staff members use their permitted view to review their own shifts and
assigned work.

220
00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:51.397
Vendors stores the businesses you use for service work.

221
00:17:51.397 --> 00:17:57.515
Add the vendor's name, trade, and contact information so you can select the
correct business on a work order.

222
00:17:57.515 --> 00:18:01.444
A vendor contact record is not the same as a signed-in vendor account.

223
00:18:01.444 --> 00:18:06.945
Use Team and access to invite a person and connect their account to the
appropriate vendor record.

224
00:18:06.945 --> 00:18:11.660
That connection allows the vendor portal to show the work assigned to that
business.

225
00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:16.312
Team and access manages individual accounts and invitations.

226
00:18:16.312 --> 00:18:22.757
Choose the appropriate role and connect a client to the correct family or a
vendor to the correct vendor record.

227
00:18:22.757 --> 00:18:29.719
Review invitation status, correct an invitation email when needed, or cancel
an invitation that should no longer be used.

228
00:18:29.719 --> 00:18:31.790
You can also suspend account access.

229
00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:37.544
Each person should use their own account so their actions and permissions
stay associated with them.

230
00:18:37.544 --> 00:18:43.240
Family-linked invitation controls are also available from the household
records we covered earlier.

231
00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:48.371
Property Records brings reference information together across homes.

232
00:18:48.371 --> 00:18:52.765
Assets and equipment is the company-wide version of the residence asset tab.

233
00:18:52.765 --> 00:19:00.338
Use it to find an asset and review identity, warranty information, service
history, and inspections without first opening its home.

234
00:19:00.338 --> 00:19:08.490
We already covered adding an asset inside a residence, so the main
distinction here is the broader view across the properties you can access.

235
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.833
Preventive maintenance stores repeat service schedules.

236
00:19:12.833 --> 00:19:18.890
Add a schedule, select the residence, and enter the maintenance description,
frequency, and next due date.

237
00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:24.719
Review due schedules and use Create due work or Run due schedules to
generate the work that is needed.

238
00:19:24.719 --> 00:19:28.890
The system is designed to generate each due visit once from its schedule.

239
00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:34.890
Keep the next due dates accurate, and manage the resulting assignment and
completion through Work orders.

240
00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:40.055
Documents collects permitted residence files in a company-wide view.

241
00:19:40.055 --> 00:19:46.468
It is another route to the files attached to each home, rather than a second
place to upload duplicate copies.

242
00:19:46.468 --> 00:19:51.016
Use clear filenames and check the residence association when adding
documents.

243
00:19:51.016 --> 00:19:56.730
Inspection and work evidence stay with their own records, which keeps this
reference list focused.

244
00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:00.414
Messages has its own place on the sidebar.

245
00:20:00.414 --> 00:20:02.957
The number beside it shows unread messages.

246
00:20:02.957 --> 00:20:08.576
Open a conversation to read and reply, or start a message to an active
account in your company.

247
00:20:08.576 --> 00:20:12.657
Use the company-wide option when the update is intended for everyone.

248
00:20:12.657 --> 00:20:19.518
Recipients receive an email notification that a message is waiting, and sign
in to read the content in Estate Aegis.

249
00:20:19.518 --> 00:20:24.190
Keep replies in the conversation so its participants can follow the
discussion.

250
00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:27.739
Use Refresh to check for new replies while the page is open.

251
00:20:27.739 --> 00:20:31.820
Company-wide replies are visible to that conversation's participants.

252
00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:38.773
Administrators can review Email activity to check recent queued
notifications and sending status.

253
00:20:38.773 --> 00:20:43.755
Use it when you need to investigate an invitation, report, or workflow
notification.

254
00:20:43.755 --> 00:20:51.525
A Sent status means the email provider accepted the message; it does not
prove that someone read it or that it reached their inbox.

255
00:20:51.525 --> 00:20:57.930
Confirm the recipient details when troubleshooting, and keep the related
account or residence email current.

256
00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:05.892
Schedules and automation provides controls for recurring work and inspection
plans, along with automation status.

257
00:21:05.892 --> 00:21:11.038
Review the assigned person, repeat interval, and next due date before
enabling a plan.

258
00:21:11.038 --> 00:21:14.809
Automation must be enabled for its scheduled processing to run.

259
00:21:14.809 --> 00:21:18.279
Keep an eye on status and due records after configuration.

260
00:21:18.279 --> 00:21:25.580
This complements staff schedules and preventive maintenance; it does not
replace reviewing assignments and completed work.

261
00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:31.138
My profile lets each person manage their own details and sign-in security.

262
00:21:31.138 --> 00:21:36.614
Review your contact information and use the available password or email
controls when needed.

263
00:21:36.614 --> 00:21:44.623
Two-factor authentication can be set up with an authenticator app by
following the on-screen steps and saving the recovery codes safely.

264
00:21:44.623 --> 00:21:47.273
It is configured separately for each account.

265
00:21:47.273 --> 00:21:52.750
Notifications is another account shortcut for reviewing in-app updates and
marking them read.

266
00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.963
Now we switch to the client portal.

267
00:21:55.963 --> 00:22:03.613
A client sees the residences assigned to their family, with a focused
overview rather than the company's internal management screens.

268
00:22:03.613 --> 00:22:11.436
They can open a residence, review published inspection reports, plan an
arrival, select saved shopping preferences, and request service.

269
00:22:11.436 --> 00:22:15.289
They can also use Messages and respond to client approval requests.

270
00:22:15.289 --> 00:22:19.603
This is where the family checks information and communicates with the team.

271
00:22:19.603 --> 00:22:25.700
The family and residence connections created during setup determine which
homes belong in this experience.

272
00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:30.776
Finally, the vendor portal gives a vendor access to assigned jobs.

273
00:22:30.776 --> 00:22:34.946
Expand a job to review its residence, manager, description, and status.

274
00:22:34.946 --> 00:22:41.524
The vendor can add a progress note, request more information, upload
evidence, and submit completion for review.

275
00:22:41.524 --> 00:22:45.812
Questions stay connected to the job so the team can respond with context.

276
00:22:45.812 --> 00:22:48.807
Vendors also have their permitted messaging access.

277
00:22:48.807 --> 00:22:52.860
They do not receive the administrator's company-wide management view.

278
00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:56.560
This keeps their workflow focused on the work assigned to them.

279
00:22:57.760 --> 00:23:00.182
That completes the Estate Aegis tutorial.

280
00:23:00.182 --> 00:23:08.509
Start with company settings, add the family, create its residence and rooms,
then build the inspections, arrivals, and work around that home.

281
00:23:08.509 --> 00:23:14.947
Use the chapter menu and the accompanying timestamp guide to return to any
section when you need a refresher.

282
00:23:14.947 --> 00:23:21.384
A demonstration company is available to explore; contact sales at estate
aegis dot com for login information.

283
00:23:21.384 --> 00:23:22.152
Estate Aegis.

284
00:23:22.152 --> 00:23:24.810
The smarter way to manage private residences.

